cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper
  (preferred-citation below) and, where relevant, this repository.
type: software
title: >-
  MNESIS: Working Memory with Polychronous Chains
abstract: >-
  MNESIS is a recurrent spiking neural network (SNN) in which every synapse
  carries D learnable delays, parameterised as a single weight tensor of
  shape N x N x D. Each stored motif is encoded as a chain of overlapping
  Spiking Motifs: contiguous context windows of length D that uniquely
  predict the next time step of activity. A closed-form initialisation,
  derived by deconvolving the LIF membrane response, is refined with
  surrogate-gradient backpropagation through time. The repository contains
  the Python implementation, the experiment notebooks and the LaTeX source
  of the paper.
